rows.en:
"............yes........."
The demon said it in a voice that seemed to make the ground groan.
And the pale blue glow grew brighter.{p}

"Don't you dare tell anyone."
They say Sawada said that to the girls who were left, and walked away.
From that night on, she was missing.{p}

"Now, Eri, sacrifice her."
The girls held down the one who was to be sacrificed.
And Sawada began to chant the incantation.{p}

The next morning, the teachers found them.
Endo wasn't among them.
When the girls came to, they rushed off to look in a mirror.{p}

In the mirror were their own familiar faces.
"Huh, it hasn't changed at all."
Sawada said that, and smiled.{p}

After that, the accidents stopped for a while.
Then there was another accident, but one of the teachers heard the rumor, and this time put a dead little bird in the incinerator and burned it.
After that, once again, there were no accidents for a while.{p}

The fire slowly caught on the trash in the incinerator and gradually spread.
Then the monsters faded away little by little.
The teacher was saved.{p}

If he didn't go this time, there was no telling what might happen again.
When he got behind the school building, he steeled himself and started walking.
His steps were heavy, and he felt like running away at any moment.{p}

"Wh-why...?"
And the sunflower that had come right up to him had Mr. Saito's face.
"M-Mr. Saito..."{p}
